{"name":"Field Day","hex":"#c5e6a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"field day","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A day for maneuvers and tactical exercises in the field (across the landscape).","A school day for athletic events."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field_day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Field day (agriculture)","blocks":[{"text":"A field day is a large trade show for agricultural industry and equipment, especially for broadacre farming. It contrasts with an agricultural show in that a show focuses on livestock and judging. A field day focuses on equipment, demonstrations and processes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Horseshoes2.jpg/330px-Horseshoes2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_day_(agriculture)"},{"title":"Field Day (amateur radio)","blocks":[{"text":"Field Day is an annual amateur radio contest, widely sponsored by IARU regions and member organizations, encouraging emergency communications preparedness among amateur radio operators. In the United States, it is typically the largest single emergency preparedness exercise in the country, with over 30,000 operators participating each year. Field Day is always the fourth full weekend of June, beginning at 18:00 UTC Saturday and running through 20:59 UTC Sunday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Camporee.JPG/330px-Camporee.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_Day_(amateur_radio)"},{"title":"Field Day (festival)","blocks":[{"text":"Field Day is a yearly outdoor music festival in London. It was first held in Victoria Park in the London Borough of Tower Hamlets on 11 August 2007 and returned there each year until 2017. The 2018 festival moved to Brockwell Park, and in 2019 it was held at Meridian Water in Enfield. Between 2021 and 2024 the festival returned to Victoria Park, and in 2025 it is to be held in Brockwell Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Field_Day_Victoria_Park20_%2835094392685%29.jpg/330px-Field_Day_Victoria_Park20_%2835094392685%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_Day_(festival)"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg/500px-Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg/1280px-Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg/500px-Field_day_IMG_3197.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"HF transceiver for voice communications","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AField_day_IMG_3197.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content